ections for the new Conservative Prime Minister Margaret Thatcher.\" That shows she was PM before 1990. Also \"The 1997 Conservative Party leadership election was triggered ... John Major resigned ...\". And \"Major had been Conservative leader and Prime Minister since November 1990.\" So we can infer that Margaret Thatcher was succeeded by John Major in 1990. But we need explicit citation that Thatcher was succeeded. Not present. However we can combine: evidence that Thatcher was PM (sentence 1) and that Major became PM in November 1990 (sentence from leadership election). That implies succession. The question: \"What United Kingdom Prime Minister was succeeded in the 1990s by the Leader of the Conservative Party?\" The answer: Margaret Thatcher. Provide citations: from \"United Kingdom local elections, 1980\" sentence 1 (Margaret Thatcher as PM) and \"Conservative Party (UK) leadership election, 1997\" sentence 1 (Major had been PM since November 1990). That shows timeline. Use those.\n\nReturn JSON with answer \"Margaret Thatcher\". citations list of pairs: [\"United Kingdom local elections, 1980\",1], [\"Conservative Party (UK) leadership election, 1997\",1]."},"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1726,"completion_tokens":663,"total_tokens":2389,"audio_prompt_tokens":0},"created":1791982402,"object":"chat.completion","prompt_filter_results":null}